166 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Why did we choose to focus on the humanitarian application of drones? The global need for humanitarian aid is immense, with an estimated 300 million people requiring assistance. The value of the aid needed is projected to be around $47 billion USD. Many of the regions in need are war-torn or lack the necessary infrastructure for aid providers to easily access those who require assistance. Disseminating aid to these areas is often prohibitively expensive or logistically impossible due to challenging terrain.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
167 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText <>
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
168 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /Figure
/P 128 0 R
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
169 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (3)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
170 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText <>
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
171 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (For UAVs to successfully deploy aid, it is crucial that they do not scatter payloads over a wide area, hoping they will be found by those in need. Instead, a more effective method involves deploying payloads directly to those who require them, particularly in regions with difficult-to-navigate terrain. Our solution to this challenge is our in-house developed machine vision software, Vision. This software has been developed using machine learning, with the model trained in various scenarios to identify, locate, and guide the drone and payload to the precise location identified by the software.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
172 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (In conclusion, the potential of drones in humanitarian efforts is vast and largely untapped. At Monash Uncrewed Aerial Systems \(MUAS\), we are committed to pushing the boundaries of what UAVs can achieve, particularly in providing critical aid to those in hard-to-reach areas. Our innovative projects, such as the lifeline system and Vision software, are testaments to our belief in the transformative power of drone technology. We hope our work not only contributes to the field but also inspires others in the industry to explore the humanitarian applications of UAVs, ultimately making a positive impact on the world.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
